201-- Prerequisite ports in this increment: `FloatPoint::tangential_points()`/`left_tangential_point()`/`right_tangential_point()` (Java `FloatPoint.tangentialPoints` etc., incl. the 90° turn for `dy > dx`), `TileShape::index_of_left_most_corner()`/`index_of_right_most_corner()`/`shrink()`, `MazeSearchAlgo::describe_expandable()`/`describe_room()` (diagnostics text), and `TargetItemExpansionDoor` fixed to own exactly one `MazeSearchElement` with `maze_search_element_count()`/`get_maze_search_element()`/`reset()` overrides — Java returns a single element there, so the C++ array-of-one emulation returned garbage and the door had no `shape_` member at all, which broke `ExpansionRoom.cpp`
202-- **Divergences, all documented in the code**: `FoundConnectionLocator::is_valid()` replaces the Java nullable `connectionItems` (a `std::vector<ItemRouteResult>` cannot be null); the dead C++ `Connectable` interface is replaced by the `is_trace()/is_via()/is_pin()/ConductionArea` guard used by `MazeSearchAlgo::calculate_target_doors`; `ExpandableObject::get_shape()` returns an `IntBox`, so the room door corners come from `get_shape_tile()`; `AutorouteDiagnostic` does not exist in C++, so all Java diagnostic callbacks are dropped
203-- **Fixture lesson recorded in the tests**: a 1-dimensional door between touching rooms has *duplicated* corners in the `IntBox` representation, so `calc_door_left_corner()`/`calc_door_right_corner()` can return the same point and the any-angle locator degenerates; real maze rooms overlap and their doors are 2-dimensional. The any-angle test therefore uses overlapping rooms (2-D doors) that are also clearly wider than twice the trace half width, because a door exactly as tall as the trace has no tangent line at all
204-- Tests: NEW `FoundConnectionLocator_test.cpp` (13 gtests), NEW `Point_test.cpp` (6 gtests for the tangential helpers), NEW `TileShape_test.cpp` (8 gtests for the corner indices and `shrink`) → **ctest 655/655 + run_tests (`AllTests`) PASSED**
205-- **Increment P (2026-10-03)**: `FoundConnectionInserter` is ported (`src/autoroute/FoundConnectionInserter.h/.cpp`, replacing the deleted `InsertFoundConnectionAlgo` stub) together with the `RoutingBoard` forced-trace prereqs `check_forced_trace_polyline()`/`insert_forced_trace_polyline()`/`insert_forced_trace_segment()`/`connect_to_trace()`/`clear_shove_failing_obstacle()`. A latent geometry divergence was fixed with it: `Polyline::Polyline(const IntPoint&, const IntPoint&)` created one line instead of Java's three (segment + two 45° stubs), which made every single-segment forced insert return its from corner. 17 new gtests (`RoutingBoardForcedTrace_test.cpp`, `FoundConnectionInserter_test.cpp`) → **ctest 707/707 + run_tests PASSED**
206-- **AutorouteEngine::autoroute_connection() wiring (2026-10-03)**: now tries the expansion-room maze path (`MazeSearchAlgo` + `FoundConnectionLocator` + `FoundConnectionInserter`) first, falling back to the legacy grid A* when the maze path fails.
207:- **Increment Q (2026-10-04)**: multi-segment (3+ corner) forced-trace insertion now works end to end. The Java-baseline comparison (the whole `java/app/freerouting` tree compiles with `javac` against the prebuilt 2.1.0 jar, so `TraceShover.insert()` / `ShapeTraceEntries.nextSubstituteTracePiece()` can be driven from a tiny harness) uncovered four real parity bugs: (1) `ShapeTraceEntries::resort()` was an approximation with an early `return` for lists shorter than two entries, so a sole own-net entry survived and made `calculate_stack_levels()` fail — it is now the full Java port (ShapeTraceEntries.java:462-573) with the `projection_approx(shape.border_line(from_side.no))` entry projection, the `prev`/`current`/`next` triplet removal, the at-most-two leading / one trailing own-net removal and `rotate_entry_list_around_anchor()`; (2) `CalcFromSide::border_intersection` is now `std::optional<FloatPoint>` (Java `ShapeEntrySide.borderIntersection` is nullable and `resort()` branches on it — the `(0,0)` sentinel was the root cause of (1)); (3) `PolylineTrace::combine()` recursed where Java loops, and `combine_at_start()`/`combine_at_end()` held a `const Point&` into `corner_points_` that `clear_derived_data()` empties, so the dangling reference crashed in `join_changed_area()` — `own_corner()` now returns an owned copy like Java's `Point startCorner = firstCorner()`; (4) `ClearanceMatrix::get_value(..., /*safety_check=*/true)` subtracted `clearance_safety_margin` where Java adds it, and `RoutingBoard::clearance_value()` (port of Java `BasicBoard.clearanceValue()`) skipped the margin, so every shove offset was 16 too small. The faithful `resort()` also changed a documented outcome: a crossing foreign trace is now shoved **around** the new shape (Java: `insert` returns `true`, one net 2 trace with corners `4000,2000 / 4000,3923 / 7077,3923 / 7077,6077 / 4000,6077 / 4000,8000`) instead of failing. 1 new gtest (`FoundConnectionInserterTest.MultiSegmentConnectionIsInserted`), `ShoveTraceAlgoInsertTest` renamed to `InsertJoinsACrossingForeignTraceAroundTheShape` and `ShapeTraceEntriesPieceTest.SubstitutePieceWrapsAroundTheShape` re-pinned to the Java numbers → **ctest 708/708 + run_tests PASSED**
208:- **Maze path wiring (2026-10-03)**: `AutorouteEngine::autoroute_connection()` now tries the expansion-room maze path (`MazeSearchAlgo` + `FoundConnectionLocator` + `FoundConnectionInserter`) first, falling back to the legacy grid A* when the maze path fails. Still missing: `AutorouteControl::fanout_start_pin_name` assignment and `ForcedViaInserter.check`'s hole-shape clearance branch (multi-segment (3+ corner) route insertion landed in Increment Q)
