## Objective
- Continue the Java → C++20 headless-routing migration by completing and documenting WP-10 Increment R fanout wiring while preserving the existing dirty working tree.
- The final migration status should remain `MIGRATION_CONTINUE` unless the entire migration, not just this increment, is verified complete.

## Important Details
- Repository: `/mnt/d/projects/EDA/freerouting_cpp`; `HEAD` is `5a56645`.
- Do not reset, discard, or overwrite the existing staged/unstaged migration work.
- Java references: `java/app/freerouting/board/facade/RoutingBoard.java:990-1122`, `java/app/freerouting/autoroute/maze/MazeSearchEngine.java`, `java/app/freerouting/autoroute/maze/MazeExpansionEngine.java`, and `java/app/freerouting/board/model/items/Pin.java`.
- `RoutingBoard::fanout(...)` is declared in the board header but defined in `src/autoroute/RoutingBoardFanout.cpp` to avoid a board-to-autoroute dependency.
- Java `retainAutorouteDatabase=false` is represented by a fresh local `AutorouteEngine`; Java’s `fallbackToBoardVias` branch remains unavailable because C++ lacks the corresponding fanout settings/global via-rule support.
- `Communication::get_resolution(Unit)` intentionally reproduces Java’s `Unit.scale` argument order, including its inverted-resolution behavior.
- `Pin::get_center()` currently uses the untransformed padstack shape for its optional center correction because C++ has no Java-style precalculated transformed pin shapes.
- The compiled `board::Components` implementation in `src/board/Component.h` is index-based and conflicts with Java’s 1-based component-ID lookup; `Pin::get_component()` follows the compiled C++ convention and documents the divergence.
- Production end-to-end fanout remains incomplete: `MazeSearchAlgo::get_instance()` still cannot create start doors for the empty/no-door harness, and other WP-10 room/start-door work remains pending.

